📊 Exploratory Data Analysis on Retail Sales Data

This project was completed as part of my Data Analytics internship at Oasis Infobyte. The goal was to perform a thorough EDA on a retail sales dataset (1,000 transactions) to uncover customer behavior, sales trends, and actionable business insights.

🔍 Key Questions Answered:

· What are the monthly and quarterly sales trends?
· Which product categories drive the most sales?
· Who are the key customer segments by age and gender?
· What correlations exist between numeric variables?

🛠️ Tech Stack:

· Python
· pandas (data manipulation)
· matplotlib & seaborn (visualization)
· Jupyter Notebook

📈 Key Insights:

· Monthly sales peak in May (~R50,000) — seasonal patterns matter
· Q4 is the strongest quarter (~R130,000)
· Clothing is the most purchased category
· Females lead in quantity sold
· Quantity is strongly correlated with Total Amount (r = 0.85)

🎯 Business Recommendations:

· Leverage seasonal peaks for targeted promotions
· Optimize inventory for top-performing categories (Clothing)
· Run campaigns targeting female shoppers
· Consider bundling products to increase quantity per transaction

